    {
      "rank": 8,
      "row_id": 293279,
      "chunk_id": "01a68cc927dc_0",
      "doc_id": "01a68cc927dc",
      "text": "Great phone - if you get the right one. The Pixel 3XL is still one of the best phones out there, especially with the camera and more processing power than the newer '3A' version. As a Techie Geek-who-can-Speak, I was especially excited to receive it! If this phone is ordered 'reconditioned' or 'used', there is a possibility that it won't work. It advertises 'unlocked' - but that isn't always the case. Like the one I received. Indeed, mine displayed 'SIM NOT FOUND' in the upper LH corner no matter which carriers SIM I put in (hey, I tried (4) different carriers for luck?). Then I tried to activate the eSIM switch, no joy either. Most of these hitting the market are former Verizon phones. Apparently, even when updated, there is a software/hardware bug in some that prevents their use. So 'unlocked' yes, most of the time? It also apparently depends on the last owner of the phone.",
      "score": 0.034810732300486404,
